  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in account ACC-1005. The details are:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (verified)\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Direction:** Outgoing card payment\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nTransaction TX-0402 also shows EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14, with the same status and type. I'm noting it only as a fact from your records.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes available in the system. Which one fits depends on what happened, which you haven't told me yet:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This may be relevant given TX-0402.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** You did not authorize a card-not-present payment (online or phone) and it was made fraudulently.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** The debit was taken from your account without your authorization.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nTell me what happened and I'll recommend the code that fits. Before any dispute is opened, I'll check its eligibility, and I'll only open it if that check passes.",
